' State Diagram 06 — finalization downward-closure (L-ANC) + the warm-path guards.
'
' The warm up-walk as a state machine:
'   Pivot F(parent) --(guards hold)--> Up-walk --(advance while finalized)-->
'   Up-walk, and --(first non-finalized)--> Highest finalized = frontier.
' Two guards (committee-constancy for L-ANC, snapshot re-check for L-SNAP) can
' trip and divert to the Cold down-walk fallback, which yields the IDENTICAL
' frontier (transparent) and emits floor_incremental_guard_fallback.
'
' Source of truth for the determinism-linchpin figure (section 3.1) in
' docs/theory/finalized-floor/finalized-floor-verification.md.
'
' Render:
'   plantuml -tsvg docs/theory/finalized-floor/diagrams/06-state-finalization-guards.puml

@startuml 06-state-finalization-guards
!theme plain

skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor<<pivot>>    #C8E6C9
  BackgroundColor<<walk>>     #BBDEFB
  BackgroundColor<<accept>>   #A5D6A7
  BackgroundColor<<fallback>> #FFE0B2
  BorderColor #444444
}
skinparam legendFontName "monospace"
skinparam legendFontSize 10
skinparam legendBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam legendBorderColor #666666
skinparam defaultFontName "monospace"
skinparam defaultFontSize 10

title Finalization downward-closure (L-ANC) and the warm-path guards

' Edge color legend:
'   green  (#2E7D32) = guards hold / normal progression
'   red    (#C62828) = guard trips → fallback
'   blue   (#1565C0) = up-walk advance
'   orange (#E65100) = stop / frontier reached
'   gray   (#546E7A) = fallback converges to the same frontier

state "Pivot F(parent)\n(finalized over just(parent))"                as Pivot    <<pivot>>
state "Up-walk\n(advance toward parent)"                              as Upwalk   <<walk>>
state "Highest finalized = frontier"                                  as Frontier <<accept>>
state "Cold down-walk (fallback)\ntop-down from parent"               as Cold     <<fallback>>

[*] -[#2E7D32]-> Pivot

Pivot   -[#2E7D32]-> Upwalk : guards HOLD ──\ncommittee constant (L-ANC)\n∧ pivot still ft_witnessed ≥ θ\nover J (L-SNAP)

Upwalk  -[#1565C0]-> Upwalk : ft_witnessed(next) ≥ θ\n⟹ advance  (amortized O(1))
Upwalk  -[#E65100]-> Frontier : ft_witnessed(next) < θ\n⟹ STOP at first non-finalized

Pivot   -[#C62828]-> Cold : committee-constancy guard TRIPS\ncommittee changed in band (bonding)\n⟹ L-ANC premise fails\n/ floor_incremental_guard_fallback
Pivot   -[#C62828]-> Cold : L-SNAP guard TRIPS\npivot no longer ft_witnessed ≥ θ\nover the larger snapshot J\n/ floor_incremental_guard_fallback

Cold    -[#546E7A]-> Frontier : top-down walk yields the\nIDENTICAL frontier (transparent)

Frontier -[#E65100]-> [*]

note top of Pivot
  L-ANC (the determinism linchpin). Under a CONSTANT committee, finalized
  blocks form a DOWNWARD-CLOSED PREFIX of the spine — the same quorum that
  finalizes a block finalizes every ancestor (GuardBridge.chain_adj_AdjDC
  derives this AdjDC premise; Floor.frontier_cache_transparent uses it).
  ⟹ warm == cold, so the cache never forks (S1).
end note

legend bottom
  L-SNAP : just(B) ⊇ just(P) ⟹ Finalized(C, just(B)) ≥ Finalized(C, just(P)) —
  the pivot stays finalized over the child's larger snapshot.
  Both guard trips are safe: the Cold fallback recomputes the SAME frontier the
  warm path would have (Rocq Floor.frontier_cache_transparent), so no fork (S1).
endlegend

@enduml
